      "content": "that's really getting there, i like the grit. it's starting to paint a much clearer hierarchy. to really hammer home that \"otherness\" i want to explore the social/cultural side a bit more. if they are this much of a different \"type\" of person compared to the elites, what would their social behaviors or cultural archetypes look like? i'm thinking about things like their communication styles, their sense of morality, or even how they view order and authority. maybe some of the \"vices\" or more primal instincts that might come out in a group that’s been pushed to this extreme? i just want to make sure they don't feel like \"polished\" people who are just poor, but like a group that has its own distinct, more \"raw\" way of existing.",
